rule section121_single_person_gain_cap with provenance "(1) In general":
the section121 single person gain cap is an amount N if
    N = 250000.

rule section121_single_person_income_excluded_from_gross_income with provenance "(1) In general":
the section121 single person income excluded from gross income is an amount if
    the section121 single person income excluded from gross income uncapped is an amount N
    and the section121 single person gain cap is an amount M
    and N >= M
    and the section121 single person gain cap is the amount
    otherwise the section121 single person income excluded from gross income uncapped is the amount.

rule section121_single_person_income_excluded_from_gross_income_uncapped with provenance "(a) Exclusion; (3) Application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years":
the section121 single person income excluded from gross income uncapped is an amount N if
    the rule section121 single person section 121 b 3 applies holds
    and N = 0
    otherwise the rule section121 single person requirements met holds
    and the section121 single person gain from sale or exchange of property is N
    otherwise N = 0.

rule section121_single_person_requirements_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 single person requirements met holds if
    the rule section121 single person requirements ownership met holds
    and the rule section121 single person requirements usage met holds.

rule section121_single_person_requirements_ownership_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 single person requirements ownership met holds if
    a number U is the sum of each N such that
        a period is in section121 single person property ownage
        and the section121 single person date of sale or exchange is a date D
            and the section121 single person begin of the period is a second date
            and a date M is 60 months after the second date
            and D <= M
            and the section121 single person begin of the period is a fourth date
            and the section121 single person end of the period is a fifth date
            and the fifth date is a number N days after the fourth date
            otherwise the section121 single person date of sale or exchange is a date K
            and the section121 single person end of the period is a date P
            and a date Q is 60 months after P
            and K >= Q
            and N = 0
            otherwise the section121 single person date of sale or exchange is a date R
            and the section121 single person end of the period is a date S
            and a date T is 60 months after S
            and T is N days after R
    and U >= 730.

rule section121_single_person_requirements_usage_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 single person requirements usage met holds if
    a number U is the sum of each N such that
        a period is in section121 single person property usage as principal residence
        and the section121 single person date of sale or exchange is a date D
            and the section121 single person begin of the period is a second date
            and a date M is 60 months after the second date
            and D <= M
            and the section121 single person begin of the period is a fourth date
            and the section121 single person end of the period is a fifth date
            and the fifth date is a number N days after the fourth date
            otherwise the section121 single person date of sale or exchange is a date K
            and the section121 single person end of the period is a date P
            and a date Q is 60 months after P
            and K >= Q
            and N = 0
            otherwise the section121 single person date of sale or exchange is a date R
            and the section121 single person end of the period is a date S
            and a date T is 60 months after S
            and T is N days after R
    and U >= 730.

